      "side": 1,
      "message": "Make sense.\n\nsupper minor question, you may ignore if it would take more than 10min)\n\nRandom idea: can we modifying FFI bindgen behavior to change type of `FDT_ERR_*`?\n\nI found that bindgen builder supports callback when converting macro into Rust type [1], and build CLI params from the bindgen builder code [2].\n\nBut I don\u0027t want to spend much time on this if you\u0027re new to this as well.\n\n\n [1]: https://docs.rs/bindgen/latest/bindgen/callbacks/trait.ParseCallbacks.html#method.int_macro\n [2]: https://docs.rs/bindgen/latest/bindgen/struct.Builder.html#method.command_line_flags",
